ressive and anxiety disorders in systemic lupus erythematosus and their association with anti-ribosomal P antibodies</article-title><source>Prog Neuropsychopharmacol Biol Psychiatry</source><year>2008</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>695</fpage><lpage>700</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18077068</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b33-ijgm-4-325"><label>33.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nery</surname><given-names>FG</given-names></name><name><surname>Borba</surname><given-names>EF</given-names></name><name><surname>Hatch</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Major depressive disorder and disease activity in systemic lupus erythematosus</article-title><source>Compr Psychiatry</source><year>2007</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>14</fpage><lpage>19</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17145276</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b34-ijgm-4-325"><label>34.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Demchuk</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Christou</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Wein</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Accuracy and criteria for localizing arterial occlusion with transcranial Doppler</article-title><source>J Neuroimaging</source><year>2000</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10666975</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b35-ijgm-4-325"><label>35.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nabavi</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><name><surname>Droste</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Kemeny</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Potential and limitations of echocontrast